# Hosting — Netlify web, Render API

This project's **web frontend** deploys on **Netlify**, not Vercel.

- Netlify site: `habiganizer`
- Production URL: `https://habitganizer.tech`
- GitHub `main` auto-build is on. After `git push` to `main`, Netlify rebuilds. Do not tell the user to sync Vercel.

The **API** is **Render** (`https://habiganize-api.onrender.com`). Netlify proxies `/api`, `/privacy`, `/support`, and `/terms` there.

If the user says "Vercel", "deploy on Vercel", or "sync to Vercel", **correct them immediately**: we build and host the web app on **Netlify**. Do not use Vercel CLI, Vercel MCP deploy tools, or set up a real Vercel app deploy.

Root `vercel.json` exists only as a **kill switch** (`git.deploymentEnabled: false` + `ignoreCommand`) so leftover Vercel↔GitHub integration does not keep failing PR checks. Do not turn it into a real Vercel deploy config. See `DEPLOY.md`.
